a^m*a^n = a^(m+n)\ "Product of Powers"
(a^m)/(a^n) = a^(m-n)m > n\ "Quotient of Powers"
(a^m)/(a^n) = 1/(a^(n-m)) m < n
(a^m)^n = a^(m+n)\ "Power of a Power"
(ab)^n = a^n b^n\ "Power of a Product"
(a/b)^n = (a^n)/(b^n) \ "Power of a Quotient"
x^3*x^5 = x^8\ "We add the exponents when multiplying."
(x^3)^5 = x^(15)\ "To raise a power to a power, we multiply exponents."
(x^3)/(x^5) = 1/(x^2) \ "To divide, we subtract exponents."
(xy)^3 = x^3 y^3\ "The power of a product is the product of the powers."
"MISTAKES"
x^3*x^5 != x^(15)\ "We should add the exponents."
(2x)^3 != 2x^3\ "2 is also cubed."
(x+2)^3 != x^3+8\ "The product rule does not apply to sums."
2*5^3 != 10^3\ "We compute powers before products."
